 "notes": "AC oscillation / cosmic-birefringence search. Headline limit on axion-photon coupling g_phigamma (identical to canonical g_agamma of L=-(g/4) a F Ftilde; Fedderke et al. convention). Curve generated from Eq. 15, the smoothed approximation to the observed 95% upper limits plotted as Keck 2012-2015 smoothed in Fig. 3: g_phigamma < 4.3e-12 GeV^-1 * sinc^-1(m/5.0e-19 eV) * (m/1e-21 eV) * (kappa*rho0/0.3 GeV/cm3)^-1/2 * (1-2(m/m0)^-2[1-cos(m/m0)])^-1/2, m0=1.9e-23 eV, with sinc(x)=sin(x)/x. Density normalization kappa*rho0=0.3 GeV/cm3 (kappa=1, i.e. axions are all DM). Mass range 1.2e-23 eV (m_min) to 5.7e-19 eV (m_max=h*nu_max, nu_max=0.5/hr). Limit degrades (turns up) at low mass near m0 (residual-oscillation factor) and would degrade at high mass via sinc. This is the observed limit (smoothed), not the expected sensitivity band.",
